WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:12.413
This is HQ, the dealer operating system. One host, one database, every module a rooftop runs on. Here it is running a two-rooftop powersports dealer.

2
00:00:13.314 --> 00:00:23.227
Tuesday morning on the desk. Units sold against goal with the pace, front and back gross, the last twenty-four hours of leads by channel, and what is ready to sell.

3
00:00:24.129 --> 00:00:34.119
Work these is customers waiting on us right now, not a list of whoever is three days old. An overnight Colebot lead, an unassigned web form, a stip that just came in.

4
00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:44.185
Leads and customers are one board. Website, Colebot, Marketplace, Messenger, phone, walk-ins. Every card carries the ad that produced it.

5
00:00:45.088 --> 00:00:54.352
Watch one arrive. Colebot qualified this customer on the website, ran a soft pull, and handed the card to the board with the unit attached and the rep alerted.

6
00:00:55.254 --> 00:01:03.103
The deal desk. Three terms across, three cash-down rows. The dark cell is the live deal, the one the contract prints.

7
00:01:04.008 --> 00:01:12.001
Tick GAP on the F and I menu and the payment, the back gross and the contract move together. GAP follows the term of the loan automatically.

8
00:01:12.904 --> 00:01:21.845
Units with readiness, not a database dump. Prepped, photographed, online, priced, days on the lot and leads, on every row.

9
00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:30.149
The service board the whole store can read. Intake to ready to sell as lanes, with the tech, the days in lane, and what is waiting on parts.

10
00:01:31.052 --> 00:01:40.608
Every unit that moves has a card. Pickups from public sellers, dealer buy runs, store transfers, deliveries tied to the signed deal, service runs.

11
00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:52.385
Your website is served straight from your inventory. A customer builds the deal at midnight, gets a real pre-approval, holds the unit with a deposit, and it lands on the desk already structured.

12
00:01:53.287 --> 00:02:02.782
Ask HQ works from your rows. What sold yesterday, how old was it, what should we go buy. It answers from your database and turns the answer into the next action.

13
00:02:03.684 --> 00:02:14.416
Scorecards you manage by. Sales, service, buying, ads and chat, with the goal and the pace next to every number. The same reports we run our own stores on.

14
00:02:15.317 --> 00:02:23.945
And it is your data. Every table exported nightly in open formats, a read API for your own tools, and no exit fees, ever.

15
00:02:24.846 --> 00:02:34.753
